---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Will Qing — personal homepage">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">PERSONAL HOMEPAGE / 2026</p>
    <h1>Hi, I’m Will Qing.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I’m an undergraduate in Information Engineering at Shanghai Jiao Tong University,
      interested in how computation can help us understand physical systems.
    </p>
    <p class="intro">
      My current research interests include optical computing, machine learning, and AI-based
      processing of physical signals. Outside research, I spend most of my time reading,
      listening to music, and, more recently, watching films.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-links">
      <a class="button dark" href="/about">More about me</a>
      <a class="button" href="#work">Selected work</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="marquee" aria-label="Current interests">
    <div>OPTICAL COMPUTING · MACHINE LEARNING · PHYSICAL SIGNALS · BOOKS · MUSIC · FILM ·</div>
  </section>

  <section id="shelf" class="section wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / THINGS I KEEP AROUND</p>
      <h2>Shelf</h2>
      <p>
        Reading, music, and film are the main things I keep returning to outside research.
        This is a small, unfinished record rather than a definitive list.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="shelf-grid">
      <article class="shelf-card">
        <figure class="shelf-visual">
          <img
            src="/images/books-library.jpg"
            alt="Rows of books in a quiet library"
            width="1280"
            height="1280"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <p class="tag">BOOKS</p>
        <h3>Books I have kept with me</h3>
        <p class="shelf-summary">
          I am drawn to quiet, humane stories about ordinary people. I also read around
          history, culture, and Song <i>ci</i> poetry.
        </p>
        <ul class="shelf-list" aria-label="Books on Will's shelf">
          <li><cite>The Unlikely Pilgrimage of Harold Fry</cite></li>
          <li><cite>A Man Called Ove</cite></li>
          <li><cite>My Grandmother Asked Me to Tell You She’s Sorry</cite></li>
          <li><cite>The Storied Life of A.J. Fikry</cite></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="shelf-future">Later: brief notes on what each book left behind.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="shelf-card">
        <figure class="shelf-visual">
          <img
            src="/images/music-turntable.jpg"
            alt="A record playing on a white turntable"
            width="1280"
            height="1917"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <p class="tag">MUSIC</p>
        <h3>A small, changing rotation</h3>
        <p class="shelf-summary">
          These are some of the artists I return to at the moment, without trying to turn
          listening into a complete profile.
        </p>
        <ul class="shelf-list compact" aria-label="Artists Will listens to">
          <li>Linkin Park</li>
          <li>Billie Eilish</li>
          <li>Ella Langley</li>
          <li>Olivia Dean</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="shelf-future">Later: albums, songs, and reasons for returning to them.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="shelf-card">
        <figure class="shelf-visual">
          <img
            src="/images/film-cinema.jpg"
            alt="Empty seats in a softly lit cinema"
            width="1280"
            height="720"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </figure>
        <p class="tag">FILM</p>
        <h3>Still learning how to watch</h3>
        <p class="shelf-summary">
          I have only recently started paying closer attention to film, so this is
          deliberately a beginning rather than a canon.
        </p>
        <ul class="shelf-list" aria-label="Recent films Will enjoyed">
          <li><cite>Spider-Man: Brand New Day</cite></li>
          <li>
            <cite>All Wishes Come True</cite>
            <span class="original-title" lang="zh-Hans">《八仙！》</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <cite>Once Upon a Time in the Middle East</cite>
            <span class="original-title" lang="zh-Hans">《欢迎来龙餐馆》</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="shelf-future">Later: short viewing notes, once I know what I want to say.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <aside class="following-strip" aria-labelledby="following-title">
      <div class="following-intro">
        <p class="tag">OTHER INTERESTS</p>
        <h3 id="following-title">Also following</h3>
        <p>A smaller corner for the teams and drivers I keep up with.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="following-item">
        <img
          src="/images/football-old-trafford.jpg"
          alt="Old Trafford seen from above"
          width="1280"
          height="959"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="tag">FOOTBALL</p>
          <h4>Manchester United</h4>
          <p>Room for match, season, and supporter notes later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="following-item">
        <img
          src="/images/f1-norris-mclaren.jpg"
          alt="Lando Norris driving a McLaren Formula 1 car"
          width="1280"
          height="853"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="tag">FORMULA 1</p>
          <h4>McLaren · Lando Norris</h4>
          <p>Room for race-weekend impressions later.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <p class="image-credits">
      Images:
      <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Library_book_stacks.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Gwyneth Perry, CC0</a>;
      <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White_turntable_playing_music_(Unsplash).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Lee Campbell, CC0</a>;
      <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Empty_Movie_Theater_Seats_(54279616742).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Eden, Janine and Jim, CC BY 2.0</a>;
      Old Trafford — Photo:
      <a href="https://arne-mueseler.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Arne Müseler / arne-mueseler.com</a> /
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/de/deed.en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">CC-BY-SA-3.0</a>;
      <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lando_Norris_2025_Italian_Grand_Prix_qualifying.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Eustace Bagge, CC BY 4.0</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="work" class="section work-section wrap">
    <div class="work-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / SELECTED WORK</p>
      <p>A few research and course projects I have worked on.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="work-list">
      <article class="work-item">
        <div class="work-meta">
          <time>2025–2026</time>
          <span>Research</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-copy">
          <h3>Optoelectronic sensing for digital pathology scanning</h3>
          <p>
            Contributed to a hybrid optoelectronic architecture designed to move focus estimation,
            acquisition anomaly warnings, and slide-quality assessment into the scanning stage.
            My work focused on differentiable optical modeling, joint optical–electronic training,
            simulation benchmarks, and parts of the scanning-control and lightweight-readout design.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="work-item">
        <div class="work-meta">
          <time>2025</time>
          <span>Course project</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-copy">
          <h3>Vision-based robotic grasping and sorting</h3>
          <p>
            Built an end-to-end system with ACT and a LeRobot SO-101 arm, covering teleoperation
            data collection, policy training, model conversion, deployment on a Moore Threads
            Yangtze SoC, and real-robot integration for sorting colored blocks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="work-item">
        <div class="work-meta">
          <time>2025</time>
          <span>Course project</span>
        </div>
        <div class="work-copy">
          <h3>Multi-view refrigerator-door angle estimation</h3>
          <p>
            Collected and annotated four-view images, trained YOLOv8-Seg to segment the door and
            key structures, and used SVD-based triangulation to reconstruct the 3D geometry and
            estimate the opening angle.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 / CURRENTLY</p>
    <h2>I’m still figuring out what deserves to stay here.</h2>
    <p>
      That is part of the point. This site is not meant to prove that I have already become something.
      It is a place to leave a trail while I’m becoming it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
